(:id "port/goose/fixed/scalar-bounds" :state :todo :evidence ("internal/codegen/goosetable/fixedform_test.go: TestGooseFixedScalarBounds/C7" "internal/codegen/goosetable/fixedform_test.go: TestGooseFixedScalarBounds/R30" "internal/codegen/goosetable/fixedform_test.go: TestGooseFixedFormAgreesWithTheByteOracle") :tested-revision "e436474479098a3906eccd2ce1023a8f76459fc2" :note "2026-11-08 STRICT-100 audit: FALSE under strict-only. <T>FixedLoad is not the strict read: it clamps a ranged scalar or a forged ordinal and counts it in report.oor instead of refusing out_of_range (docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md section 4.6), and lands a bool or present byte other than 0 or 1 as true instead of refusing wire_damaged (section 4.5). The cited tests assert that clamping and those counters, the proof suite's C++ oracle reads TableReport fields the strict cut removed (clamped, kind_mismatch, duplicate, malformed), and the goose fixedform and versioning negative controls are red on main run 42459510328 at e254a5cba. Earlier: 2026-11-03: Goose fixed-form code fix (PRs #2734 and the fixedform branch it carries); tests read the C++ reference corpus build/fixedform-corpus. Every cited test re-run on vision (Linux x86-64, pinned goose v2026.2) at main e43647447: 379 TestGooseFixed* events pass.")
